# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined tp4/window-next four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/window-next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# O1 (AUDITED ATTACH, LEAN, the first octo attach): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-octo-audit, QWEN_FAST_OCTO=alternate with the verify T1/T2 audits and the extent audit. Two tests only: warmup and concurrent8_steady (nine requests). An audited
# 8x262k request costs about 8.4 minutes, so the octo pack's seven-test A1 (about 35 requests, 150 minutes) is cut to the one test the octo rule needs: eight live users past the draft window, which is
# where at least 16 octo rounds and at least 16 counted rounds of each shape, strictly alternating, come from. No A0 control: the audited text-equality read is P3 against P1 (octo_compare, unaudited),
# and the audits themselves (T1, T2, extent) are exact on the octo shape or the run fails. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the attach: '[OCTO] admitted mode=alternate rows=8 users=8 min_live=6
# (gate only)' once, the UNQUALIFIED lines, no '[OCTO] refused'; no program compiled after the attach; DRAM after attach as the memory plan says (the pool gave back 3,468 blocks to the third block: an allocation
# failure at its construction is the named memory risk, tp4-octo-jobs/ORDER.txt); '[PINDIAG] extent replay engaged segments=8 flags=0x21,...,0x21 ... geometry=G8B1' and the '[QWEN-SDPA] runtime-extent entries=1
# kv_share=false' factory line; '[PINDIAG] tp4 vglue octo 8-row served path' (not a FALLBACK); (2) c2_smoke_check clean, whose octo rule judges the log (octo_judge.judge): at least 16 octo rounds at rows=8, at least 16
# counted rounds of EACH shape alternating strictly, no program compiled on a switch, zero audit mismatch (T1, T2, extent) on either shape. NO text comparison here (no audited control ran). Duration (estimate): 90 minutes
# (nine audited requests at 8.4 minutes, plus a boot).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-octo-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
